 # CSG Difference
-Also called: SDF Difference, Subtraction of SDFs, CSG Subtraction
+Also called: SDF Difference, Subtraction of SDFs, CSG Subtraction, difference
 ## Overview
 The CSG Difference operation constructs a new Signed Distance Function (SDF) by subtracting one shape from another, effectively carving the first object out of the second [S1, unofficial, S2, unofficial]. Unlike the standard union (minimum) in [Constructive SDF Modeling (Min Combination)](871-constructive-sdf-modeling-min-combination.md), which merges volumes, this operation removes the volume of the subtractor from the base, ensuring the resulting field represents the solid region of the base that does not overlap with the subtractor [S1, unofficial].
