 ## Background
-The CSG Difference is a fundamental operation in Constructive Solid Geometry (CSG) applied to Signed Distance Fields [G]. It is widely used in procedural geometry generation and ray marching shaders to create complex scenes from simple primitives [G]. The method relies on the property that the distance to the union of two shapes is the minimum of their distances, and the distance to the difference is the maximum of the base distance and the negated subtractor distance [S1, unofficial, S2, unofficial]. Origin and historical development are not given in the sources.
